      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ba749f34dca6b351d658330|full_name}: A PC is much, much more powerful than any standalone VR headset. You can't just say they should have the same experience when they simply arent the same. VRC is already quite taxing on the Quest with its currently VERY restricted limits.\nThe main issue is, VRChat is a very unpredictable environment. Worlds have vasty different performances on Quest, and player count within a lobby is unpredictable too. They have to set the limits in a way that works in the worst possible scenarios for overall stability for every user.\nThat is just the way it has to be, no surprise since its mobile hardware. And not even the most powerful mobile hardware availble. The latest 2022 smartphone flagships are much more powerful than a Quest 2 for example.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
