      "mergeID": "6619385ef5cbdbb1d027d9e1",
      "mergedPostDetails": "So Avatar's on PC have audio right?\nWhat if we could have audio on quest as well?\nThis would be a really awesome feature for quest!!!\nimagine being able to toggle audio on and off for both platforms.\nLike say if you wanted to listen to a certain audio on an avatar but you can't because your on Quest.\nI think this would be a feature loved by all of VRchat's Quest user's like myself.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Audio for Quest avatars",
      "parentID": "634de753902794562a1c35ea",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6045c21f30eaac39db24433e",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62631f154aa573528f523a41|full_name}: This is not to say that they should offer the exact same experience.\nCertainly VRChat is very unstable compared to other social VR platforms, but I do not think that is a reason to give up on efforts to support Quest.\nIn particular, VRChat, along with the aforementioned props non-support, has left cross-platform support completely up to the user, and that policy is unlikely to change in the future. If that is the case, I think that the interface for that should be provided to users.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
