      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Allowing Quest users to hear audio from avatars in VRChat would significantly improve the overall user experience and accessibility of the platform. Currently, many avatars include custom audio features that enhance interaction, roleplay, and creative expression. However, these features are often unavailable to users on the standalone Quest version, creating an uneven experience between platforms. Implementing support for avatar-based audio on Quest devices would help ensure that all users can participate more fully in shared virtual spaces. It would also encourage creators to continue developing innovative avatars without worrying about platform limitations. By expanding compatibility, VRChat could strengthen its reputation as an inclusive and community-driven virtual environment. Additionally, consistent audio functionality would improve immersion and social engagement for Quest users. This change could also help bridge the gap between PC and standalone users within the same worlds. As the Quest user base continues to grow, supporting more avatar features will become increasingly important. For these reasons, enabling avatar audio on Quest would be a valuable and forward-thinking improvement for the VRChat platform.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
